From c51c7dc758954ce944ec26862d192152813796bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Clarke <sanity@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Feb 2026 10:36:12 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 06/69] fix: add delegate migration entry before stdlib 0.1.40
 publish (#119)

* fix: add delegate migration entry for pre-stdlib-0.1.40 WASM

PR #115 bumped freenet-stdlib from 0.1.35 to 0.1.40, which changes the
delegate WASM bytecode and therefore the delegate key. Without a migration
entry, users' room data stored under the old delegate key becomes
inaccessible after redeployment.

Add V3 entry to LEGACY_DELEGATES with the key computed from the delegate
WASM built with stdlib 0.1.35 / scaffold 0.2.2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

* fix: extend legacy migration TODO date to 2026-06-01

The previous date (2026-03-01) was only 2 days away, which would have
made the V3 migration entry dead code before users could migrate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

---------

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
